                  <msItem>
                     <title>Mapheus Vegius, De significatione verborum (4 fols.)</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Two bifolia removed from Savile N. 12 (Petrus
                        Nonius, etc., 1573), where they were in use as binding leaves (Oxford
                        binding, s. xvi ex.). Ker, Pastedowns, no. 1454.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Presumably the copy seen at Balliol by Leland
                        (Collectanea 4, 61).</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">The combination of roman hand and English
                        ornament suggests a close relation with Balliol MSS. 287 (part) and 310 --
                        both given to the College by Richard Bole, archdeacon of Ely -- which stand
                        next to the Mapheus Vegius in Leland's list.</note>
                  </msItem>
